Passage: DIR, Annex II, 1

[0] 1.
[1] CONTENT A.
[2] EC DECLARATION OF CONFORMITY OF THE MACHINERY This declaration and translations thereof must be drawn up under the same conditions as the instructions (see Annex I, section 1.7.4.1(a) and (b)), and must be typewritten or else handwritten in capital letters.
[3] This declaration relates exclusively to the machinery in the state in which it was placed on the market, and excludes components which are added and/or operations carried out subsequently by the final user.
[4] The EC declaration of conformity must contain the following particulars:
[5] 1.
[6] business name and full address of the manufacturer and, where appropriate, his authorised representative;
[7] 2.
[8] name and address of the person authorised to compile the technical file, who must be established in the Community;
[9] 3.
[10] description and identification of the machinery, including generic denomination, function, model, type, serial number and commercial name;
[11] 4.
[12] a sentence expressly declaring that the machinery fulfils all the relevant provisions of this Directive and where appropriate, a similar sentence declaring the conformity with other Directives and/or relevant provisions with which the machinery complies.
[13] These references must be those of the texts published in the Official Journal of the European Union;
[14] 5.
[15] where appropriate, the name, address and identification number of the notified body which carried out the EC type-examination referred to in Annex IX and the number of the EC type-examination certificate;
[16] 6.
[17] where appropriate, the name, address and identification number of the notified body which approved the full quality assurance system referred to in Annex X;
[18] 7.
[19] where appropriate, a reference to the harmonised standards used, as referred to in Article 7(2);
[20] 8.
[21] where appropriate, the reference to other technical standards and specifications used;
[22] 9.
[23] the place and date of the declaration;
[24] 10.
[25] the identity and signature of the person empowered to draw up the declaration on behalf of the manufacturer or his authorised representative.
[26] B.
[27] DECLARATION OF INCORPORATION OF PARTLY COMPLETED MACHINERY This declaration and translations thereof must be drawn up under the same conditions as the instructions (see Annex 1, section 1.7.4.1(a) and (b)), and must be typewritten or else handwritten in capital letters.
[28] The declaration of incorporation must contain the following particulars:
[29] 1.
[30] business name and full address of the manufacturer of the partly completed machinery and, where appropriate, his authorised representative;
[31] 2.
[32] name and address of the person authorised to compile the relevant technical documentation, who must be established in the Community;
[33] 3.
[34] description and identification of the partly completed machinery including generic denomination, function, model, type, serial number and commercial name;
[35] 4.
[36] a sentence declaring which essential requirements of this Directive are applied and fulfilled and that the relevant technical documentation is compiled in accordance with part B of Annex VII, and, where appropriate, a sentence declaring the conformity of the partly completed machinery with other relevant Directives.
[37] These references must be those of the texts published in the Official Journal of the European Union;
[38] 5.
[39] an undertaking to transmit, in response to a reasoned request by the national authorities, relevant information on the partly completed machinery.
[40] This shall include the method of transmission and shall be without prejudice to the intellectual property rights of the manufacturer of the partly completed machinery;
[41] 6.
[42] a statement that the partly completed machinery must not be put into service until the final machinery into which it is to be incorporated has been declared in conformity with the provisions of this Directive, where appropriate;
[43] 7.
[44] the place and date of the declaration;
[45] 8.
[46] the identity and signature of the person empowered to draw up the declaration on behalf of the manufacturer or his authorised representative.
